%let $H$ be the bipartite subgraph of $G$ with $V(H)=I'\cup K'$ and $E(H)=\{uv\in E(G) : u\in I', v\in K'\}$. Let $C$ be an induced cycle in $H$ such that $V(K)\setminus V(C)\ne\emptyset$. We refer to $C$ in $H$ as a short cycle in $G$, if such a cycle exists.
