The Step‑0 discriminator is already decisive against Track A: the paper’s own class is exactly an efficiently solvable side of a published dichotomy—Hamiltonian cycle is polynomial-time on \(K_{1,3}\)-free and \(K_{1,4}\)-free split graphs. I’m now inspecting that cited algorithm and its cost to determine whether a defensible Track B family exists; I will not present worst-case Hamiltonicity as hardness for this distribution.
