Thus, any vertex in $K$ has at least two neighbors in $I$.
As $G$ is claw-free, it follows that $|I|=3$.
So $G$ has structure as displayed in Fig. \ref{f2}, so
$G$ contains a Hamiltonian cycle $u_3Pu_1Qu_2Ru_3$, where $P$, $Q$, $R$ are  Hamiltonian paths in
$G[N_G(u_1)\cap N_G(u_3)]$, $G[N]$, $G[N_G(u_2)\cap N_G(u_3)]$, respectively. This is
a contradiction.
\end{proof}

