codex
Implemented a native Track B Hamiltonian-cycle generator based on the paper’s \(K_{1,4}\)-free split graphs and Theorem 1.2. Track A was ruled out because Hamiltonian cycle is polynomial-time solvable for this class, as established by the cited [Renjith–Sadagopan dichotomy](https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.00855).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2604_14763.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.14763/gen_2604_14763.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.14763/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.14763/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.14763/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.14763/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.14763/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: each 0/8.
- Reference blossom algorithm: 8/8, averaging 14,690 operations.
- Shipping answer: 236 atoms, 1,070 characters, 473 conservative tokens.
- Compact route: 282 exact arithmetic operations.
- Canonical-key invariance: 20/20; unrelated distinctness: 20/20.

The required oracle hardening remains blocked: all bare, structural-hint, and placebo calls returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The transcripts are genuine harness-produced error records, not hardness evidence. After replenishing the OpenRouter account, Step 4 and the three G9 arms must be rerun before submission.

I also removed the temporary emitted dataset artifact created during validation; all requested deliverables remain. The mathematical choices and the oracle blocker are documented in the README, with reference to the [full source paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2604.14763v1).
